│                                     ┌ volumes backup ─ minecraft-flk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐                                     │
│                                     │ Copy volumes (default: all of the app's) to the backup dir, then prune old       │                                     │
│                                     │ copies                                                                           │                                     │
│                                     │ · How the app is kept from writing comes from [flk.backup] in flk.toml (see flk  │                                     │
│                                     │   help --all): by default its machine is stopped for the copy and started again; │                                     │
│                                     │   mode = "live" with pre/post hooks (e.g. save-off / save-on) copies while it    │                                     │
│                                     │   runs.                                                                          │                                     │
│                                     │ · Copies are sparse, and instant on XFS/btrfs when the backup dir shares the     │                                     │
│                                     │   volume's filesystem. The copy is checked with e2fsck (a copy of a running      │                                     │
│                                     │   machine gets its journal replayed).                                            │                                     │
│                                     │                                                                                  │                                     │
│                                     │ app         [minecraft-flk▏                                                    ] │                                     │
│                                     │             the app (-a); the selection's app by default                         │                                     │
